title: military_tower_context
---
// Garrison of the Iron Bastion (military_tower), planned to move into the
// Gate Authority dimension. The annex remains attached in the intended
// layout; room connections are a separate level-design task.
// The General speaks through military_general in factions.yarn.
// Never played. No placement names this node.
===

title: military_tower_voss
---
Casey: EYES FRONT. Keep clear of the parade deck when the squad is drilling.
-> What do you drill here?
    Casey: Formations, guard changes, weapons handling. Half my recruits have only worked civilian gate posts.
-> Do your recruits travel through the gates?
    Casey: Some do. The first time out, I give them a good long rest after the crossing. Nobody takes a rifle on watch while they're seeing double.
-> Fall out.
===

title: military_tower_dorsey
---
Dorsey: Halt! Oh, a visitor. Carry on if you're here to see the General.
-> What is through the annex door?
    Dorsey: The gate annex. The checkpoint opens for clearance only, and clearance comes from the General.
    Dorsey: The checkpoint has a maintenance crawlway underneath. I am supposed to keep an eye on it as well.
-> Have you been posted here long?
    Dorsey: Six months. Used to work on a civilian gate. Lot more visitors there, but nobody made me salute every time the door opened.
    Dorsey: I keep a copy of arrivals for the signals floor. Nobody told me the civilians needed one too.
-> Carry on, Private.
===

title: military_tower_tanaka
---
Tanaka: Off duty. Can you pass me my boots? The clean pair.
-> What do you do on duty?
    Tanaka: Night watch on the signals floor. If somebody dials the annex, I have to alert the sentry and check that Ruiz got the address on the tape.
-> Do you get much leave?
    Tanaka: I'm meeting my sister in the Concourse when my watch ends. She gets sick coming through the ring, so I'll go with her to find something to eat.
-> Leave her to it.
===

title: military_tower_bankole
---
Bankole: Corporal Bankole. You can sit on the bunk if you want. Don't wake Tanaka if she nods off.
-> What's life like in the garrison?
    Bankole: Fine. I can visit the shops on leave. The civilians are always asking me to help carry their suitcases. I suppose it's the uniform.
-> Why the beret?
    Bankole: My old regiment's. It's against the barracks dress code. Brandt hasn't spotted it yet.
-> As you were.
===

title: military_tower_granger
---
Granger: Quartermaster's counter. Bring your kit here for inspection before you sign it back in.
-> What can I draw from the armory?
    Granger: Nothing without a chit. The chits are upstairs. The forms for the chits are downstairs. Welcome to the army.
-> Where do you get the equipment?
    Granger: We order parts from all over. Half the requisitions on my desk are waiting for freight. One supplier in PVN sent me a very polite apology and no boots.
-> Never mind.
===

title: military_tower_ruiz
---
Ruiz: Signals. Every dial of the annex ring prints a line on my tape.
-> What can you learn from the tape?
    Ruiz: Which gate called, and when the connection closed. I need the sentry's report to know who walked through it.
    Ruiz: Major Brandt asked me for a second copy for the Manifest Office. I told him the same tape twice won't tell the registrar who was on the other side.
-> Who dialed today?
    Ruiz: Two test calls from a public ring. The General wanted to check that the printer works. It works.
-> Back to your tape.
===

title: military_tower_brandt
---
Brandt: Major Brandt, adjutant. The General sees visitors on the hour.
-> When is the hour?
    Brandt: Now. It is always the hour. He does not own a watch, and nobody has volunteered to give him one.
-> What are those papers?
    Brandt: Duty rosters and correspondence with the Manifest Office. The civilians have requested another copy of the annex logs. I sent a copy yesterday.
    Brandt: Ruiz tells me they want the sentry's report as well. That is not what the letter said. I suppose I had better ask Dorsey for it.
-> Is the General here all day?
    Brandt: Unless he's inspecting the troops. If he leaves the tower for a meeting at the Authority, I have to go with him and carry the papers.
-> Thank you, Major.
===
